TEXT -1208 56 Left 6 ;TESTING:\nEarth fault on Phase1\nSee the voltage at the petbus\nbefore and later\nThe voltage L1-N is before fault 65.5kV\nThe voltage at the petbus is at faulttime 63.5kV \nwhich is a little bit smaller as the full voltage\nThe reason is due to the inner impedance of the\nfirst transformer (three samephased currents to the \npetersen(s) flows through the primary windings of\ntransformer 1)\nYou can see (by deleting the shunt reactor)\nthat no current flows from transformer 2 to the\npetersen(s). The only current is the magnetizing\ncurrent of the secondary side of transformer 2 which is also fed from\ntransformer 1
TEXT 272 -56 Left 4 ;The current from the voltage source lags the voltage (Delivering of inductive reactive load)\nDelivering for the shunt reactor is partly from the feeding voltage source and partly from the capacitances of the two lines\nYou can see that the current of the line is smaller at the begin and\nbigger at the end of the line because of delivering reactive current from the line capacitances of the line to the\nshunt reactor
TEXT -344 232 Left 2 ;The fault current is high \nat the begin and goes \nin direction of zero
TEXT -232 -160 Left 5 ;Testcircuit with feeding the shunt reactor  in oposite direction
TEXT -1208 600 Left 5 ;HINT: If the switcher Sw_3Phase_off_i0 (open at current < i0) \ndoes not open you can make i0 higher but if there are spikes in the simulation\nyou can also let i0 (or make it smaller) and also make the minimal timestep of .tran statement smaller \nso the i0 parameter can better met the condition
